course: dictionary
lesson: 7422
title: A serious illness: polio
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Polio is an illness caused by a virus, which is a tiny germ. It is serious because it can damage the nerves, the messages that travel between your brain and your muscles.
explain: When nerves are damaged, a person can become paralysed, which means they cannot move part of their body. The full name of polio is poliomyelitis.
explain: Polio is an uncountable noun, so we talk about polio itself, not "a polio". Context helps: «Polio can cause paralysis» tells you that polio is a serious illness, even if you did not know the word before.
fact: Polio is a serious illness caused by a virus.
fact: «Polio can cause paralysis.» Paralysis means being unable to move part of the body.
fact: Vaccines against polio have made the illness rare.
fact: The wild polio virus is still found mainly in Pakistan and Afghanistan.
fact: The full name of polio is poliomyelitis.
exercise: Polio is a serious illness caused by what? | A cold wind | *A virus | A broken bone | Too much sugar
exercise: «Polio can cause paralysis.» What does paralysis mean? | Being very tired after running | *Being unable to move part of the body | Being able to fly | Feeling cold in winter
exercise: «There are vaccines against illnesses such as measles, polio and flu.» Find and copy the full name of polio, which is not in this sentence. | vaccination | polio virus | *poliomyelitis | paralysis
test: Vaccines against polio have made the illness what? | Louder | Wetter | Stronger | *Rare
test: According to the example, where is the wild polio virus still found mainly? | London and Paris | *Pakistan and Afghanistan | Australia and Canada | Scotland and Wales
exam: Using context, which best explains polio? | A new game played on phones | A type of vaccine that cures colds | A kind of sweet food from Pakistan | *A serious illness caused by a virus that can damage nerves
